abstract:
The third family of ensembles. Bagging averages, boosting corrects, stacking learns how to combine. A second-level model is trained on the out-of-fold predictions of several different base learners, so it can discover that one model is reliable in one region and another elsewhere. We build the out-of-fold matrix by hand, show exactly how in-sample predictions leak, and measure why diversity matters more than individual accuracy.}
